    <briefdescription>
<para>Concept satisfied by two pointers, one of which points to a function. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The comparison of a function pointer with an object pointer, such as a <computeroutput>void*</computeroutput>, is an extension of the compilers, accepted with a warning, which the library silences, but not by the checks of the concepts that follow; the comparators keep accepting it.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Lhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the left hand side operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Rhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the right hand side operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
